<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>JouleLab</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('nav') %>

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow mono">JOULELAB · ENERGY MEASUREMENT</p>
      <h1>JouleLab</h1>
      <p class="sub">Per-module energy measurement for embedded boards. INA219 current sensing on an STM32 NUCLEO-F446RE; target: ESP32.</p>
      <dl class="facts">
        <div><dt>SENSOR</dt><dd>INA219, high-side shunt, I²C · 0.1 mA resolution · 532 µs averaging</dd></div>
        <div><dt>MEASUREMENT MCU</dt><dd>STM32 NUCLEO-F446RE · binary packets over ST-LINK USB serial</dd></div>
        <div><dt>SAMPLE RATE</dt><dd class="mono">500 Hz (team firmware) · 1.88 kHz (profiler.ino)</dd></div>
        <div><dt>PHASE TIMING</dt><dd>Firmware markers (JL_FUNCTION_START/END) or GPIO edges on A0/A1</dd></div>
        <div><dt>SEPARATION</dt><dd>Spectrogram + NMF on one current trace</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <div class="cta"><a class="btn-p" href="#live">Live hardware</a><a class="btn-s" href="#sim">Simulator</a><a class="btn-s" href="/workspace">Workspace</a></div>
    </div>
    <figure class="fig">
      <div class="scope">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 600 220" class="chart" role="img" aria-label="Modelled ESP32 current over the first second of one cycle">
          <g stroke="#1f2421"><line x1="48" x2="590" y1="194" y2="194"/><line x1="48" x2="590" y1="148.5" y2="148.5"/><line x1="48" x2="590" y1="103" y2="103"/><line x1="48" x2="590" y1="57.5" y2="57.5"/><line x1="48" x2="590" y1="12" y2="12"/></g>
          <g class="tick" text-anchor="end"><text x="42" y="200">0</text><text x="42" y="154">50</text><text x="42" y="109">100</text><text x="42" y="63">150</text><text x="42" y="18">200</text></g>
          <g class="tick" text-anchor="middle"><text x="48" y="216">0</text><text x="183.5" y="216">0.25</text><text x="319" y="216">0.50</text><text x="454.5" y="216">0.75</text><text x="575" y="216">1.00 s</text></g>
          <text x="54" y="28" class="tick">mA</text>
          <polyline points="48.0,193.9 58.8,193.9 58.8,172.2 102.2,172.2 102.2,148.5 264.8,148.5 264.8,27.4 285.1,52.4 305.5,27.4 325.8,52.4 346.1,27.4 366.4,52.4 386.8,27.4 407.1,52.4 427.4,44.0 427.4,193.9 590.0,193.9" fill="none" stroke="#e5a50a" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="mono small"><span>FIG. 1 · SIM · ESP32 standard cycle, first 1.0 s of 10 s</span><span>sense → process → Wi-Fi TX → sleep</span></figcaption>
      <table class="mono">
        <tr><th>VOLTAGE</th><td>3.30 V</td></tr>
        <tr><th>CURRENT · AVG / PEAK</th><td>7.28 mA / 183.1 mA</td></tr>
        <tr><th>POWER · AVG</th><td>24.02 mW</td></tr>
        <tr><th>ENERGY / CYCLE</th><td>240.2 mJ</td></tr>
        <tr><th>SOURCE</th><td>SIM model, not a measurement</td></tr>
      </table>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="sec how" id="how">
    <div class="sec-h"><h2><span class="n">1</span> Setup</h2></div>
    <p class="lead">INA219 in the supply path of the board under test; the NUCLEO timestamps each sample and streams it to the backend.</p>
    <div class="grid2">
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><span class="n">1.1</span><div><b>Measure the supply</b><p>INA219 in series with the target's supply: bus voltage and shunt current. Sample rate and shunt range set the shortest transient you can resolve.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="n">1.2</span><div><b>Label the phases</b><p>Wrap each firmware phase in begin/end markers, or toggle A0/A1, so every sample maps to the code that drew it.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="n">1.3</span><div><b>Re-measure after each change</b><p>Keep board, cycle interval and battery assumptions fixed so before/after numbers are comparable.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="n">1.4</span><div><b>Replace modelled phases</b><p>Run separation on recorded sessions or imported logs; the simulator is only a reference.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="code-panel scope">
<pre class="mono">EB_BEGIN("sensing");
read_sensor();
EB_END("sensing");

<span class="cm">// markers are timestamped and matched
// against the measured supply current</span></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div id="root"></div>

  <section class="sec esp" id="esp32">
    <div class="sec-h"><h2><span class="n">4</span> Reference: ESP32</h2></div>
    <p class="lead">Datasheet-typical figures. Module revision, supply, firmware and antenna change real values; measure your board.</p>
    <div class="grid2">
      <div>
        <dl class="spec">
          <% esp32.specs.forEach(function (s) { %><div><dt class="mono"><%= s[0].toUpperCase() %></dt><dd><%= s[1] %></dd></div><% }) %>
        </dl>
        <div class="btns"><a class="btn-s" href="/workspace">Check ESP32 sketch</a><a class="btn-s" href="#sim">Simulate ESP32</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="modes">
        <p class="mono small">CURRENT BY POWER MODE · LOG SCALE</p>
        <% esp32.modes.forEach(function (m) { %><div class="mode"><span><%= m[0] %></span><div class="b"><i style="--w:<%= (Math.log10(m[2]) / Math.log10(300000) * 100).toFixed(1) %>%"></i></div><b class="mono"><%= m[1] %></b></div><% }) %>
        <p class="tip mono"><%= esp32.tip %></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec take">
    <div class="row">
      <div><div class="sec-h"><h2><span class="n">5</span> Report</h2></div>
        <p class="lead">Text report of the current simulator settings: phases, average and peak current, cycle energy, projected runtime.</p></div>
      <a class="btn-s dl mono" id="report" href="/api/report">Download report (.txt)</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script src="/vendor/react/react.production.min.js"></script>
  <script src="/vendor/react-dom/react-dom.production.min.js"></script>
  <script>window.BOARDS = <%- JSON.stringify(boards) %>;</script>
  <script src="/js/app.js"></script><!-- compiled from src/app.jsx by `npm run build` -->
</body>
</html>
